#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# memory_constrained

#% text
# `memory_constrained(e, b)` evaluates `e` allocating at most `b` bytes.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is the value of `e` if evaluating it allocates at most `b` bytes; otherwise the evaluation is stopped (or its value dropped) and the value is `failure(limit, memory)`.

#% item
# `memory_constrained(e, b, fail)` evaluates `fail` instead of giving the failure.

#% item
# The bytes counted are those the evaluation adds to the heap, and the size of the value itself; the measure is coarse for small amounts.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
memory_constrained(range(100), 100, "too much memory")
#% output
#= "too much memory"

#% cell
memory_constrained(range(5), 10^6)
#% output
#= [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `time_constrained`, `pause`
